Build the complete component script.

Retail payment processing in Guatemala, Central America: all monetary amounts are in Guatemalan quetzales (GTQ).

Copy payment_ref. Trim settlement_text; null/empty is MISSING, an invalid strict yyyy-MM-dd date in UTC is INVALID, otherwise VALID with canonical yyyyMMdd stored in settlement_key. settlement_key is null unless valid. Use locale en.US.

Normalize outlet_code by trimming and uppercasing; use null for blank. outlet_check is MISSING for blank, INVALID unless the normalized value starts with "GT-" and has at least six characters, OK otherwise.

charge_check is MISSING for null sale_total, INVALID for sale_total <= 0, OK otherwise.

funding_check is MISSING for null received_total, INVALID for received_total < 0, UNCHECKED if charge_check is not OK, SHORT if received_total < sale_total, EXACT if equal, OVER otherwise. Apply these checks in the stated order.

Null cashier_confirmed means false; store the normalized boolean in confirmation_flag.

Count one problem for each of:
- settlement_check is not VALID;
- outlet_check is not OK;
- charge_check is not OK;
- funding_check is neither EXACT nor OVER;
- funding_check is OVER and confirmation_flag is false.

Set processing_lane to HOLD when there is any problem, CHANGE_DUE when there are no problems and funding_check is OVER, CAPTURE otherwise.

Component: REFORMAT.
